var tafsirData_78 = {
  "1": "\"What are they asking one another about?\" opens Surah an-Naba with a question about the deniers’ conversation. The question mirrors the earlier rushing to mock and groups to mock.\n\n“What are they asking one another about?” translates the inquiry about the momentous news, over which they disagree, but no! They will come to know, again no! They will come to know, have We not smoothed earth like a bed, mountains as pegs, created you in pairs, sleep for rest, night as cover, day for livelihood, built seven mighty heavens, placed a shining lamp, sent down pouring water, producing grain, plants, dense orchards, and the Day of Decision is an appointed time. What are they asking indicates the deniers’ dispute, like the deniers who asked “When is the Day?” mockingly and thought Allah would not resurrect.\n\nAsking one another is the same as secret talks that grieve, whispering to exclude poor, and rushing headlong to mock.\n\nThis follows “So what message after this Quran would they believe in?” to show that even after the most complete message, they still ask, but now about the momentous news, the same news that winds and angels warned about, the promised will come to pass.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear asking as sincere inquiry, like the sensible one who urged “say Allah willing.” This asking is argumentative, as with those who felt secure that earth will not swallow.\n\nFor the believer who has been shown the Way grateful or ungrateful, what they ask should be answered with the reminder that surely this is a reminder, so let whoever wills take the Right Way, and with the call to worship Allah alone, fear Him, obey, so asking becomes the righteous’ asking one another in Gardens about the wicked, not the deniers’ asking about momentous news in dispute.",
  "2": "\"About the momentous news,\" answers “What are they asking about?” The news is the resurrection and judgment they deny.\n\n“About the momentous news” translates “‘an al-naba’ al-‘azim,” the great news, the same news that winds sent, angels distinguishing, and delivering warn about, ending excuses and giving warnings. Momentous, or “‘azim,” is great, as with the Blessed in Whose Hands rests all authority and He is Most Capable, the Greatest whose Name is to be glorified, and the weighty revelation soon sent. Momentous news is the Day of Decision, the Inevitable, the Striking, the Day the sky will be torn frail, the Trumpet, the presented with no secrets hidden, the Gardens and Fire.\n\nThis follows what are they asking to name it, and precedes over which they disagree, showing that the news is disputed, as with the deniers who thought they would not be resurrected and the challenger demanding punishment.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to reduce momentous news to a news bulletin, like caravan fanfare that drew crowds from the pulpit. Momentous news is the ultimate truth, the absolute truth, whose woe is repeated for deniers.\n\nFor the living, momentous news should be taken as reminder, not dispute. Take the Right Way while you will, be among those in awe without seeing whose mighty reward is forgiveness, so momentous news becomes your Gardens held in honour where you are told to eat and drink happily, not the Fire’s roaring as it boils over and fury almost bursting.\n\nAdditional: Momentous news, or “naba’ ‘azim,” also is the same news that winds sent and angels distinguishing and delivering warn about, ending excuses and giving warnings. Momentous news is the weighty Day, the Inevitable, the Striking, the Day fifty thousand years they see as far but We see as near, the difficult Day far from easy, the dunes, and the sky split. Momentous news is the ultimate truth, the absolute truth, whose woe is repeated for deniers. For the living who are told this is a reminder so let whoever wills take the Right Way, momentous news should be taken as reminder, not dispute, so momentous news becomes your Gardens held in honour where you are told to eat and drink happily, not the Fire’s roaring as it boils over and fury almost bursting.",
  "3": "\"over which they disagree.\" describes the deniers’ stance toward the momentous news. The disagreement is not sincere.\n\n“over which they disagree” translates “alladhi hum fihi mukhtalifun,” that they are in differing about, disputing, as with the deniers who said ancient fables, pure magic, word of a man, and how can humans be guides, and who rushed headlong to mock from right and left in groups. Disagree here is not healthy reasoning, but denial, like pressing fingers, covering clothes, persisting, acting arrogantly, and devising tremendous plot urging idols.\n\nThis follows momentous news to show that the news is disputed, and precedes “But no! They will come to know,” indicating that disagreement will be resolved by knowledge.\n\nDisagreement contrasts with the angels fully distinguishing truth from falsehood and delivering to end excuses; the delivered was clear, but they disagreed.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to equate disagreement with legitimate scholarly difference, as with the better garden hoped for after turning. Disagreement here is about the resurrection itself, not details.\n\nFor the believer who has been shown the Way grateful or ungrateful, disagreement should be replaced by gratitude, fulfilling vows, giving food despite desire, and fearing the sweeping horror, so disagreement is not yours, but the Gardens where you ask about the wicked with gratitude are yours.\n\nMore: Over which they disagree also includes the pagans’ dispute about the Quran’s source—poet, fortune-teller, magic, ancient fables—and about “How can humans be guides?” and about oaths binding until the Day. Disagree here is denial, like the hypocrites who hinder with false shields and the garden owners who left no thought for Allah’s Will. The angels fully distinguishing truth from falsehood already separated, but they disagree. To not disagree, be among those who believed the amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance, who will never associate, and who are properly observant, whose Gardens are held in honour, where disagreement is replaced by Gardens asking one another about the wicked with gratitude.",
  "4": "\"But no! They will come to know.\" warns the disagreeing deniers after asking about momentous news. The denial is emphatic.\n\n“But no! They will come to know” translates “kalla sa-ya‘lamun,” No! Soon they will know, as with the garden reduced to ashes while they slept, the blast for Thamud, the wind for ‘Ad, and the stern grip for Pharaoh, all ways of Our punishment in this world far worse in Hereafter if only they knew, and the severe punishment prepared. Will come to know indicates knowledge will arrive, as with soon you and the pagans will see which is mad, and the Day they will be presented with no secrets hidden and all informed of what they sent forth, despite excuses.\n\nBut no, or “kalla,” is the same denial of their disagreement, as with “But no! There will certainly be a raging Flame,” and “But no! By the moon, Hell is mightiest catastrophe.”\n\nThis follows over which they disagree to state that disagreement will be resolved by knowledge, not by debate, as with the keepers asking “Did a warner not come?” and they reply “Yes, but we denied.”\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear “will come to know” as future threat only, not present lesson, like the despicable withholder who thought wealth prevents knowing. Knowing now through the reminder is possible, as with attentive ears that grasp the Ark.\n\nFor the living who love fleeting and neglect weighty Day, will come to know should prompt taking the reminder now, so knowing is the bright faces looking at their Lord, not the gloomy anticipating devastation, and the Day they will come to know is the elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach, not the woe on that Day to deniers.\n\nFurther: But no! They will come to know also parallels the garden reduced to ashes while they slept, the blast for Thamud, the wind for ‘Ad, and the stern grip for Pharaoh, all ways of Our punishment in this world far worse in Hereafter if only they knew. Will come to know, or “sa-ya‘lamun,” indicates knowledge will arrive inevitably, as with soon you and the pagans will see which is mad, and the Day they will be presented with no secrets hidden and all informed. But no denies disagreement, as with “But no! There will certainly be a raging Flame” and “But no! By the moon, Hell is mightiest catastrophe.” For the wrapped who stands at night reciting properly, will come to know is the promise that Gardens held in honour will be known, not the deniers’ woe.",
  "5": "\"Again, no! They will come to know.\" repeats the warning with emphasis after “But no! They will come to know.” Doubling underscores certainty.\n\n“Again, no! They will come to know” translates the same as before, repeated for stress, like the double condemnation for contemplating a degrading label, the double woe for the denier who neither believed nor prayed, and the double “Woe to you, and more woe, Again woe.” Repetition hammers that the momentous news disputed will be known, whether you disagree, rush to mock, or love fleeting and neglect weighty Day.\n\nAgain indicates that the second knowing may be more intense, as with the presentation where no secret stays hidden and the informing of what was sent forth and left behind, and as with the Day the soul reaches collar bones and no healer saves.\n\nThis follows But no! They will come to know to intensify, and precedes “Have We not smoothed out the earth like a bed,” giving the signs that make knowing possible now.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to tire of repetition, like those who turned away from the reminder as spooked zebras. Repetition is mercy, as with the reminder that would humble a mountain and the Pen.\n\nFor the believer, again they will come to know should make you among those who already know now, who were in awe without seeing, whose mighty reward is forgiveness, who walk upright, so knowing is not the woe on that Day to deniers, but the knowledge that “All this is surely a reward, your striving appreciated” and the vast kingdom and bliss are yours.\n\nExtra: Again, no! They will come to know repeats for stress, like the double condemnation for contemplating a degrading label, the double woe for the denier, and the double “Woe to you, and more woe.” Repetition hammers that the momentous news disputed will be known, whether you disagree, love fleeting, or neglect weighty Day. Again indicates second knowing may be more intense, as with presentation where no secret stays hidden and informing of what was sent forth. For the believer, again they will come to know should make you among those who already know now, who were in awe without seeing, whose mighty reward is forgiveness, so knowing is not the woe on that Day to deniers, but the knowledge that “All this is surely a reward, your striving appreciated” and the vast kingdom and bliss are yours.",
  "6": "\"Have We not smoothed out the earth ˹like a bed˺,\" begins the list of signs after warning they will come to know. The earth smoothed is the first sign.\n\n“Have We not smoothed out the earth like a bed” translates “alam naj‘ali al-arda mihada,” did We not make earth a bed, a cradle, like the earth a lodging for the living and the dead, the earth smoothed for you to move about and eat from provision, the earth spread for spacious pathways, and the earth made very easy for him who was created alone and became hungry for more. Smoothed like a bed, or “mihada,” is a prepared, comfortable expanse, as with the bed for the living and the dead, the lodging.\n\nHave We not is rhetorical expecting “Yes, indeed, You did,” as with the humble fluid placed in secure place until appointed time, perfectly ordained, and the mountains as pegs, and the shining lamp, and the pouring rain.\n\nThis follows Again they will come to know to show what they will know, the signs that prove the momentous news is true.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to take smoothed earth as denying mountains as pegs next. Smoothed is the surface for lodging and walking, pegs are stabilization, both from the Most Capable who holds all authority.\n\nFor the one created from humble fluid, earth smoothed like a bed should make you grateful, show Way, choose grateful, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, so smoothed bed becomes Gardens held in honour where you recline on canopied couches never seeing scorching heat, not the dunes of shifting sand on the Day earth and mountains shake.\n\nMore: Smoothed out the earth like a bed also echoes the earth a lodging for the living and the dead, the earth smoothed for you to move about and eat from provision, the earth spread for spacious pathways, and the earth made very easy for him who was created alone and became hungry for more. Smoothed like a bed, or “mihada,” is a prepared, comfortable expanse, opposite to the dunes of shifting sand when earth and mountains shake, and the Fire that does not let live. For the one created from humble fluid, earth smoothed like a bed should make you grateful, show Way, choose grateful, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, so smoothed bed becomes Gardens held in honour where you recline on canopied couches never seeing scorching heat, not dunes.",
  "7": "\"and ˹made˺ the mountains as ˹its˺ pegs,\" continues the signs after earth smoothed. Mountains as pegs stabilize.\n\n“and made the mountains as its pegs” translates “wa al-jibala awtada,” mountains as stakes, pegs, as with towering firm mountains and fresh water to drink, the mountains blown away like tufts of wool, dunes of shifting sand, and the mountains as pegs that prevent earth from shaking violently. Pegs, or “awtad,” are stakes that anchor, like the Pen’s precise measure and the well-preserved Record.\n\nThis follows smoothed earth like a bed to show that the bed is stabilized, not swallowing as it quakes violently for those who feel secure.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think mountains as pegs contradicts mountains blown away. Pegs stabilize for the appointed time until the Day of Decision set, then they are blown away as part of the promise will come to pass.\n\nFor the living who are over-occupied by day with worldly duties, mountains as pegs should inspire awe of Majesty who created you in stages, seven heavens, moon, sun, growth like plant, and spread pathways, so you are not among those who persist in denial and act very arrogantly, but among those who take the Right Way, recite what is easy, and are among the bright faces looking at their Lord, where pegs become the shade right above and fruit easy.\n\nFurther: Mountains as pegs also contrasts with towering firm mountains and fresh water to drink, the mountains blown away like tufts of wool, dunes of shifting sand, and the mountains as pegs that prevent earth from shaking violently. Pegs, or “awtad,” are stakes that anchor, like the Pen’s precise measure and the well-preserved Record. The One who smooths bed and pegs mountains is the Most Capable who holds all authority. For the living over-occupied by day, mountains as pegs should inspire awe of Majesty who created you in stages, seven heavens, moon, sun, growth like plant, and spread pathways, so you are not among those who persist in denial and act very arrogantly, but among those who take the Right Way, recite what is easy, and are among the bright faces looking at their Lord, where pegs become shade right above and fruit easy.",
  "8": "\"and created you in pairs,\" adds human pairing after earth and mountains. Pairs include male and female produced from the clot, the two sexes, and the pairs of all creation.\n\n“and created you in pairs” translates “wa khalaqnakum azwaja,” We created you as pairs, as with producing from it both sexes, male and female, the pair from the drop, the clot, the perfected form. Pairs, or “azwaja,” also includes sleep and rest as pairs, night as cover and day for livelihood, and the Gardens where you will be amid cool shade and springs.\n\nCreated you in pairs follows mountains as pegs to show that the One who stabilizes earth also creates companionship, not isolation like no close friend on the Day the sky is molten brass.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to limit pairs to marriage without seeing the broader pairing as mercy, like the Balance so people may administer justice and the Pen.\n\nFor the one who was nothing worth mentioning, then a drop for test, created in pairs should make you grateful, show Way, choose grateful, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, so pairs become the Gardens where you recline and the vast kingdom where you are not alone but held in honour with companions, not the worthless planks leaned that impress but are plank-like alone.\n\nMore: Created you in pairs also includes sleep and rest as pairs, night as cover and day for livelihood, and the Gardens where you will be amid cool shade and springs. Pairs, or “azwaja,” shows mercy, as with the Balance so people may administer justice and the Pen. Created in pairs follows mountains as pegs to show that the One who stabilizes earth also creates companionship, not isolation like no close friend on the Day the sky is molten brass. For the one who was nothing worth mentioning, then a drop for test, created in pairs should make you grateful, choose grateful, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, so pairs become the Gardens where you recline and the vast kingdom where you are not alone but held in honour with companions, not the worthless planks leaned that impress but are plank-like alone.",
  "9": "\"and made your sleep for rest,\" gives the next sign after pairs. Sleep is mercy.\n\n“and made your sleep for rest” translates “wa ja‘alna nawmakum subata,” We made your sleep a rest, a cut off, as with the night worship more impactful, the wrapped and covered at night, and the over-occupied day. Sleep for rest, or “subata,” is to disconnect, to repose, like the garden owners slept while torment struck and reduced it to ashes, but for the grateful, sleep is mercy that restores, not punishment.\n\nThis follows created in pairs to show that pairing includes rest, and precedes night as cover and day for livelihood, forming the daily cycle that the Lord of east and west determines.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to take sleep for rest as mere biology, not as sign. Sleep for rest is a daily mini-death and resurrection, as with the soul reaching the throat while you are looking on and the Day all will be informed.\n\nFor the human created from humble fluid, sleep for rest should remind you of the Day you will be presented with no secrets hidden, where sleep is not, but Gardens where you never see scorching heat or bitter cold and are waited on with silver vessels is the final rest. Use sleep gratefully, remember the Name morning and evening, prostrate part of night, glorify long, so sleep for rest becomes the elevated Garden’s reclining on canopied couches, not the raging Flame that rips scalps.\n\nExtra: Made your sleep for rest also restores, like the garden owners slept while torment struck and reduced it to ashes, but for the grateful, sleep is mercy that restores, not punishment. Sleep for rest, or “subata,” is to disconnect, to repose, like the night worship more impactful, the wrapped and covered at night, and the over-occupied day. Sleep for rest follows created in pairs to show that pairing includes rest, and precedes night as cover and day for livelihood, forming the daily cycle that the Lord of east and west determines. Use sleep gratefully, remember the Name morning and evening, prostrate part of night, glorify long, so sleep for rest becomes the elevated Garden’s reclining on canopied couches, not the raging Flame that rips scalps.",
  "10": "\"and made the night as a cover,\" continues the daily cycle after sleep for rest. Night as cover is protection and privacy.\n\n“and made the night as a cover” translates “wa ja‘alna al-layla libasa,” We made night as clothing, covering, as with the night more impactful and suitable for recitation, the night as it retreats sworn by, the wrapped and covered, and the over-occupied day. Cover, or “libasa,” is to clothe, to conceal, like garments purified and the Garden’s silk garments, but here darkness covers, giving rest and concealment, as with the Pen and what everyone writes covered in the well-preserved Record.\n\nThis follows sleep for rest to show night’s function, and precedes day for livelihood, completing the pair.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think night as cover is merely darkness to fear, like the Fire’s dark smoke three columns. Night as cover is mercy, like the Garden’s shade right above, not the Fire’s smoke that provides neither coolness.\n\nFor the one who was nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, night as cover should inspire devotion wholeheartedly, as with standing half the night reciting properly, taking Trustee, and being patient with what they say and departing courteously, so cover becomes the Gardens’ canopied couches where never seeing scorching heat, not the choking food and painful punishment in store for luxury deniers left for a little while.\n\nFurther: Made the night as a cover also shows the night more impactful and suitable for recitation, the wrapped and covered at night, and the over-occupied day. Cover, or “libasa,” is to clothe, to conceal, like garments purified and the Garden’s silk garments, but here darkness covers, giving rest and concealment, as with the Pen and what everyone writes covered in the well-preserved Record. Cover is mercy, like the Garden’s shade right above, not the Fire’s smoke that provides neither coolness. For the one who was nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, night as cover should inspire devotion wholeheartedly, as with standing half the night reciting properly, taking Trustee, and being patient with what they say and departing courteously, so cover becomes Gardens’ canopied couches where never seeing scorching heat, not choking food.",
  "11": "\"and made the day for livelihood,\" completes the daily cycle after night as cover. Day for livelihood is activity.\n\n“and made the day for livelihood” translates “wa ja‘alna al-nahara ma‘asha,” We made day for seeking life, as with moving about the smoothed earth’s regions and eating provision, dispersing after Friday to seek bounty and remember often to be successful, and the Messenger’s day over-occupied with worldly duties, weighty revelation, and standing half the night. Livelihood, or “ma‘ash,” is to live, to seek, as with abundant rain, gardens, rivers, wealth and children supplied after seeking forgiveness, and the excellent provision granted to those who believe and do good.\n\nThis follows night as cover to show that dark and light both serve, as with the sun as radiant lamp and moon as reflected light within seven heavens.\n\nDay for livelihood is the time of sabhan tawila, long occupation, where remembering the Name wholeheartedly and devoting still apply.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to take day for livelihood as excuse to love fleeting and neglect weighty Day ahead, like the despicable withholder and luxury deniers indulging until they face their Day.\n\nFor the grateful who fulfil vows, fear sweeping horror, and give food despite desire, day for livelihood becomes the days gone by for which you are told to eat and drink happily, where livelihood was earned lawfully with rightful share, making room, and protecting families, so livelihood becomes Gardens held in honour where livelihood is the vast kingdom and bliss, not the raging Flame that summons hoarders who gathered and hoarded.\n\nMore: Made the day for livelihood also completes the daily cycle after night as cover. Day for livelihood is activity, as with moving about the smoothed earth’s regions and eating provision, dispersing after Friday to seek bounty and remember often to be successful, and the Messenger’s day over-occupied with worldly duties, weighty revelation, and standing half the night. Day for livelihood, or “ma‘ash,” is to live, to seek, as with abundant rain, gardens, rivers, wealth and children supplied after seeking forgiveness. Livelihood is test, as with fleeting world neglected, the despicable withholder, and luxury deniers indulging until they face their Day. For the grateful who fulfil vows, day for livelihood becomes the days gone by for which you are told to eat and drink happily, where livelihood was earned lawfully with rightful share, making room, and protecting families, so livelihood becomes Gardens held in honour.",
  "12": "\"and built above you seven mighty ˹heavens˺,\" returns to cosmic signs after daily cycle. Seven mighty heavens are the canopy.\n\n“and built above you seven mighty heavens” translates “wa banayna fawqakum sab‘an shidada,” We built above you seven strong, mighty, as with seven heavens one above another without flaw where sight returns frustrated, created for a purpose, He shaped you perfecting form, and to Him is final return, the well-preserved Record, and the Lord of pathways on a Day fifty thousand years. Mighty, or “shidada,” is strong, powerful, like the Blessed in Whose Hands rests all authority Most Capable, the King, Holy, Almighty whose Hands hold authority, and the formidable severe angels over the Fire.\n\nBuilt above you indicates the heavens are a constructed canopy, like the roofing of a lodging earth, bed, and pegs, showing the One who lodged living and dead also roofs with seven mighty.\n\nThis follows day for livelihood to show above, and precedes shining lamp and pouring rain.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to see seven mighty heavens as mythic. They are the flawless creation you are told to look again at without finding flaw, now built mighty.\n\nFor the one created from humble fluid, seven mighty heavens should make you in awe of Majesty, not in awe of idols Wadd and Nasr, so you seek forgiveness, showered with rain, supplied with wealth, given gardens, and take the Right Way with recitation what is easy, establishing prayer, paying alms, lending good loan, and seeking forgiveness, so built above you becomes the Gardens held in honour where the mighty heavens are not torn but are your canopy’s promise fulfilled as Gardens where fruit hangs within reach.\n\nExtra: Built above you seven mighty heavens also returns to the seven heavens one above another without flaw where sight returns frustrated, created for a purpose, He shaped you perfecting form, and to Him is final return, the well-preserved Record, and the Lord of pathways on a Day fifty thousand years. Mighty, or “shidada,” is strong, powerful, like the Blessed in Whose Hands rests all authority Most Capable, the King, Holy, Almighty. Built above you indicates the heavens are a constructed canopy, like the roofing of a lodging earth, bed, and pegs, showing the One who lodges living and dead also roofs with seven mighty. For the one created from humble fluid, seven mighty heavens should make you in awe of Majesty, so you seek forgiveness, showered with rain, supplied with wealth, given gardens, and take the Right Way with recitation what is easy, establishing prayer, paying alms, lending good loan, and seeking forgiveness, so built above you becomes Gardens held in honour where the mighty heavens are not torn but are your canopy’s promise.",
  "13": "\"and placed ˹in them˺ a shining lamp,\" details one of the seven mighty heavens’ adornments after building them. The lamp is the sun.\n\n“and placed in them a shining lamp” translates “wa ja‘alna sirajan wahhaja,” We placed a blazing lamp, the sun as radiant lamp, as with placing the moon as reflected light and sun as radiant lamp within seven heavens, the shining lamp that delights planters with rain then withers to chaff, and the sun and moon brought together on the Day sight is stunned.\n\nShining lamp, or “sirajan wahhaja,” is blazing, glowing, as with the stars like lamps as missiles for devils, the Pen, and the reminder.\n\nThis follows seven mighty heavens to show their lamp.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to worship the lamp, as with idols. Lamp is created, like the moon’s reflected light, whose Lord is east and west, no god except Him, take Him as Trustee.\n\nFor the grateful, shining lamp should remind you to look again at flawless heavens without finding flaw, to see birds held, to take the Right Way, so lamp becomes your Gardens’ never seeing scorching heat, where lamp’s heat is tempered, and your faces are bright looking at their Lord, whose light you perfectly seek.\n\nFurther: Placed in them a shining lamp also details one of the seven mighty heavens’ adornments after building them. The lamp is the sun as radiant lamp, as with placing the moon as reflected light and sun as radiant lamp within seven heavens, the shining lamp that delights planters with rain then withers to chaff, and the sun and moon brought together on the Day sight is stunned. Shining lamp, or “sirajan wahhaja,” is blazing, glowing, as with the stars like lamps as missiles for devils, the Pen, and the reminder. For the grateful, shining lamp should remind you to look again at flawless heavens without finding flaw, to see birds held, to take the Right Way, so lamp becomes your Gardens’ never seeing scorching heat, where lamp’s heat is tempered, and your faces are bright looking at their Lord, whose light you perfectly seek.",
  "14": "\"and sent down from rainclouds pouring water,\" gives the next sign after shining lamp. Rain from clouds is provision.\n\n“and sent down from rainclouds pouring water” translates “wa anzalna min al-mu‘sirati ma’an thajjaja,” We sent down from the rain-laden clouds water gushing. Pouring, or “thajjaja,” is abundant, copious, as with abundant rain showered after seeking forgiveness, gardens and rivers supplied, spring flowing at will, flowing water if yours sinks who could bring it, and the rain that delights planters. Rainclouds, or “mu‘sirat,” are squeezed, pressed to rain, like the Pen pressed to write and the Record.\n\nThis follows shining lamp to show that lamp’s heat drives rain, the sun evaporates sea water left behind as salt and returns as sweet, showing the One who makes water sweet if He wills from clouds or salty, and who smooths earth, pegs mountains, creates pairs, sleep, night, day, heavens, lamp, now rain.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to take pouring water as mere weather, not as mercy and test, like the garden test.\n\nFor practice, sending down pouring water should move you to seek forgiveness, so He showers abundant rain, and to be among those who give rightful share, let the poor enter your garden today, so pouring becomes your Gardens’ springs and rivers under which rivers flow for ever and ever, where pouring is excellent provision granted to those who believe and do good, not the flood that overflowed where We carried you in the Ark for the rebellious, nor the choking food.\n\nMore: Sent down from rainclouds pouring water also gives the next sign after shining lamp. Rain from clouds is provision. Pouring, or “thajjaja,” is abundant, copious, as with abundant rain showered after seeking forgiveness, gardens and rivers supplied, spring flowing at will, flowing water if yours sinks who else could bring it, and the rain that delights planters. Rainclouds, or “mu‘sirat,” are squeezed, pressed to rain, like the Pen pressed to write and the Record. This follows shining lamp to show that lamp’s heat drives rain, the sun evaporates sea water left behind as salt and returns as sweet, showing the One who makes water sweet if He wills from clouds or salty. For practice, pouring water should move you to seek forgiveness, so He showers abundant rain, and to be among those who give rightful share, let the poor enter your garden today, so pouring becomes your Gardens’ springs and rivers under which rivers flow for ever and ever, where pouring is excellent provision granted to those who believe and do good.",
  "15": "\"producing by it grain and ˹various˺ plants,\" states the effect of pouring water after sending it down. Grain and plants are provision.\n\n“producing by it grain and various plants” translates “li-nukhrija bihi habban wa nabata,” to bring forth with it grain and vegetation, as with the sowing “is it you who cause it to grow or is it We?” and the rain that delights planters then withers to chaff, and the garden reduced to ashes while they slept. Grain and plants are the harvest that could be chaff leaving you to lament “we have been deprived” and the provision from sources never imagined.\n\nProducing by it indicates the same One who placed humble fluid in secure place until appointed time and perfectly ordained, who smoothed earth, and who built seven heavens, produces.\n\nThis follows pouring water to show result.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to credit rain alone, not the Producer, like the despicable’s ancient fables because blessed with wealth.\n\nFor the grateful who fulfil vows, fear sweeping horror, and give food despite desire, grain and plants become the Gardens’ any fruit they desire, told to eat and drink happily, rewarded as good-doers, where grain is not the garden’s fixated early harvest but the Gardens’ easy fruit, and dense orchards of the next verse.\n\nExtra: Producing by it grain and various plants also shows the effect of pouring water, as with the sowing “is it you who cause it to grow or is it We?” and the rain that delights planters then withers to chaff, and the garden reduced to ashes while they slept. Grain and plants are the harvest that could be chaff leaving you to lament “we have been deprived” and the provision from sources never imagined. Producing by it indicates the same One who placed humble fluid in secure place until appointed time and perfectly ordained, who smoothed earth, and who built seven heavens, produces. To avoid crediting rain alone, remember the Producer, be grateful, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, so grain and plants become the Gardens’ any fruit they desire, told to eat and drink happily, rewarded as good-doers, where grain is not the garden’s fixated early harvest but the Gardens’ easy fruit, and dense orchards of the next verse.",
  "16": "\"and dense orchards?\" completes the earth and heavens signs after grain and plants. The orchards are lush, intertwined.\n\n“and dense orchards?” translates “wa jannatin alfafa,” gardens, orchards, entangled, dense, as with the garden owners’ garden, the helpers’ gardens and rivers, the Gardens of Bliss with their Lord, the elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach, and the Gardens under rivers for ever and ever where excellent provision is. Dense, or “alfafa,” is thick, interwoven, showing abundance, like the vast kingdom and bliss.\n\nThis follows grain and plants to show that pouring water produces not only staple grain but also dense orchards, the complete provision, as with the beautiful names and the Pen.\n\nDense orchards are the earthly foretaste of the Gardens held in honour, shade right above, silver vessels, crystal, ginger, Salsabil, eternal youths, vast kingdom, fine silk, silver bracelets, pure drink.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to see dense orchards as mere scenery for those who love fleeting and neglect weighty Day.\n\nFor the one who was nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown grateful or ungrateful, dense orchards should make you grateful, fulfilling vows, feeding despite desire, so dense orchards become your Gardens held in honour where dense is not dunes of shifting sand but the Garden’s shade right above and fruit easy, where you recline on canopied couches never seeing scorching heat, and where your striving has been appreciated.\n\nFurther: Dense orchards also completes the earth and heavens signs after grain and plants. The orchards are lush, intertwined, dense, as with the garden owners’ garden, the helpers’ gardens and rivers, the Gardens of Bliss with their Lord, the elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach, and the Gardens under rivers for ever and ever where excellent provision is. Dense, or “alfafa,” is thick, interwoven, showing abundance, like the vast kingdom and bliss. Dense orchards are the earthly foretaste of the Gardens held in honour, shade right above, silver vessels, crystal, ginger, Salsabil, eternal youths, vast kingdom, fine silk, silver bracelets, pure drink. To see dense orchards as mere scenery for those who love fleeting and neglect weighty Day is to miss the sign. For the one who was nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown grateful or ungrateful, dense orchards should make you grateful, fulfilling vows, feeding despite desire, so dense becomes your Gardens held in honour where dense is not dunes but the Garden’s shade right above and fruit easy.",
  "17": "\"Indeed, the Day of ˹Final˺ Decision is an appointed time—\" confirms the Day after describing earth lodging, mountains, fresh water, and dense orchards. The Day is appointed.\n\n“Indeed, the Day of Final Decision is an appointed time—” translates the Day set, for which stars put out, sky torn, mountains blown, messengers timed, Day set, woe to deniers, earlier and later destroyed, humble fluid secure, perfect ordainment, earth lodging, mountains pegs, pairs, sleep, night, day, heavens, lamp, rain, grain, orchards, all prepare. Appointed time, or “miqat,” is the same miqat as earlier and later generations gathered for appointed Day, the appointed time that never delays, the appointed time for humble fluid in secure place, and the Day fifty thousand years.\n\nIndeed, or emphatic, shows the promise will come to pass is not the powerless force that would help, the honour that expels, or merchandise, but the Pen.\n\nThis follows dense orchards to show that dense, like lodging, is for the appointed.\n\nAppointed time— with dash indicates the next verses detail what appointed entails, Trumpet blown, crowds, sky gates, mountains mirage, Hell ambush.\n\nFor the one who was nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, grateful or ungrateful, the appointed time should make you grateful, fulfilling vows, fearing sweeping horror, giving food despite desire, so appointed is Gardens for you, not the Fire’s endless ages where no coolness or drink except boiling water and pus.\n\nFurther, appointed time— with dash shows the next verses will detail the Trumpet, crowds, sky gates, mountains mirage, Hell ambush, home for transgressors, endless ages, no coolness, boiling pus, fitting reward, never expecting reckoning, totally rejecting signs, precise recording, taste more torment, salvation, Gardens, vineyards, maidens, full cups, no idle talk, generous gift. Appointed time is the momentous news they disagree over, but no, they will come to know, again no. For the one created from humble fluid, appointed time should make you grateful, fulfilling vows, giving food despite desire, so appointed is Gardens for you, not the Fire’s pleasant punishment in store for those left to Me.",
  "18": "\"˹it is˺ the Day the Trumpet will be blown, and you will ˹all˺ come forth in crowds.\" details the appointed time. The Trumpet and crowds are central.\n\n“it is the Day the Trumpet will be blown, and you will all come forth in crowds” translates the first event of the appointed, the Trumpet blown with one blast after which earth and mountains crushed and Inevitable has come to pass, sky torn frail, angels on sides, Throne borne by eight, you presented with no secrets hidden. Trumpet, or “sur,” blown is the same as the garden reduced to ashes while they slept as a visitation, the blast for Thamud, wind for ‘Ad, stern grip for Pharaoh.\n\nCome forth in crowds, or “afwaja,” in groups, indicates the gathering as with the Day He will gather you all for mutual loss and gain, every soul detained except people of the right, and the Day fifty thousand years.\n\nAll indicates every earlier and later disbeliever, humble fluid placed, perfect ordainment.\n\nThis follows appointed time to show what appointed is.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think crowds are chaotic, like rushing headlong to mock from right and left. Crowds here are for Final Decision, not mocking, as with angels fully distinguishing.\n\nFor the living who love fleeting and neglect weighty Day, come forth in crowds should prompt taking the Right Way while you will, reciting what is easy, so coming forth is with the righteous amid cool shade and springs, any fruit they desire, told to eat and drink happily, not with the transgressors where Hell is lying in ambush as a home.\n\nMore, Trumpet blown and crowds coming forth also fulfills the Day the soul reaches collar bones and feet tied and you are driven to your Lord, the mustaqarr, where all are informed of what was sent forth and left behind, despite excuses, where people testify against own souls. Trumpet blown is the same as the garden reduced to ashes while they slept as a visitation, the blast for Thamud, wind for ‘Ad, stern grip for Pharaoh, all ways of Our punishment in this world far worse in Hereafter. Crowds coming forth indicates the gathering as with the Day He will gather you all for mutual loss and gain, every soul detained except the people of the right, and the Day fifty thousand years. To be among crowds told to eat and drink happily, be among the righteous amid cool shade and springs, not the transgressors where Hell is lying in ambush.",
  "19": "\"The sky will be ˹split˺ open, becoming ˹many˺ gates,\" gives the second sign of the appointed time after the Trumpet and crowds. The sky becomes gates.\n\n“The sky will be split open, becoming many gates” translates the sky torn, split, as with the sky torn frail with angels on its sides, sky like molten brass, sky split apart and His promise must be fulfilled, sky will even turn children’s hair grey, sky torn, and seven heavens without flaw where sight returns frustrated now split.\n\nMany gates, or “abwaban,” are openings, like the Garden’s vast kingdom and bliss where gates are many, but here gates for the Inevitable, the angels descending, the Throne, and the presentation.\n\nSky split to gates indicates the heavens’ flawless creation without flaw now opens, as with the Pen’s writing and the well-preserved Record opened.\n\nThis follows Trumpet and crowds to show cosmos gate.\n\nSky split should not be taken as mere weather, but as the Inevitable’s gate for judgment where you will be presented.\n\nFor the wrapped who stands half the night reciting properly, sky split open as many gates becomes your gates to Gardens where fruit hangs within reach, not the gates to Hell lying in ambush.\n\nExtra: Sky split open, many gates also recalls the sky torn frail with angels on its sides and eight bearing the Throne, the sky like molten brass, the sky that will even cause children’s hair to turn grey, His promise must be fulfilled, the sky torn. Many gates, or “abwaba,” are openings for angels descending, for judgment, as with the Garden’s vast kingdom and bliss where gates are many, but here gates for the Inevitable. Sky split to gates indicates the heavens’ flawless creation without flaw now opens, as with the Pen’s writing and the well-preserved Record opened. Sky split should not be taken as mere weather, but as the Inevitable’s gate for judgment where you will be presented, and the wrapped who stands half the night reciting properly will find gates to Gardens where fruit hangs within reach, not gates to Hell lying in ambush.",
  "20": "\"and the mountains will be blown away, becoming ˹like˺ a mirage.\" gives the third sign, mountains as mirage, after sky gates. The firm becomes illusion.\n\n“and the mountains will be blown away, becoming like a mirage” translates mountains blown, scattered, becoming mirage, or “saraba,” like a shimmer, as with mountains blown away like tufts of wool, dunes of shifting sand, earth and mountains lifted and crushed, mountains like uprooted palm trunks for ‘Ad. Mirage indicates the mountains appear but are not, like the powerless force that would help, the honour that expels inferior, and the merchandise fanfare.\n\nBlown away, or “suyyirat,” is to be moved, as with the garden fixed early purpose blown to ashes.\n\nThis follows sky gates to show earth’s pegs removed.\n\nMountains as mirage shows that what seemed firm, like strongholds that put them out of reach, is now illusion.\n\nFor the one created from humble fluid placed in secure place, mountains blown to mirage should humble, as with looking again at flawless heavens without finding flaw, now seeing mountains blown, so you are not among deniers woe on that Day, but among the righteous who will have salvation, Gardens, vineyards, full-bosomed maidens, full cups, never hearing idle talk or lying, a reward as generous gift from your Lord, where mountains are not mirage but Gardens’ shade right above.\n\nFurther: Mountains blown away, mirage also recalls the mountains as pegs, towering firm mountains and fresh water, the mountains blown away like tufts of wool, dunes of shifting sand, and the mountains as pegs. Mirage, or “saraba,” like shimmer, shows the mountains appear but are not, like the powerless force that would help, the honour that expels inferior, and the merchandise fanfare. Blown away shows no stronghold puts you out of reach, no wealth and children divert, and no honour expels. For the one created from humble fluid placed in secure place, mountains blown to mirage should humble, as with looking again at flawless heavens without finding flaw, now seeing mountains blown, so you are not among deniers woe on that Day, but among the righteous who will have salvation, Gardens, vineyards, full-bosomed maidens, full cups, never hearing idle talk, a reward as generous gift from your Lord, where mountains are not mirage but Gardens’ shade right above.",
  "21": "\"Indeed, Hell is lying in ambush\" reveals what lies beyond the mirage mountains and gated sky on the appointed Day. Hell waits.\n\n“Indeed, Hell is lying in ambush” translates “inna Jahannama kanat mirsada,” Hell is a watch, an ambush, lying in wait, as with the Fire that almost bursts, raging Flame ripping scalps, Saqar not letting live, scorching skin, nineteen keepers, mighty catastrophe warning to humankind, and the difficult Day far from easy. Mirsada is a place of observation, a trap, like the garden owners’ garden watched while they slept and torment struck, and the despicable withholder watched.\n\nLying in ambush indicates Hell is prepared, ready, as with chains, shackles, blazing Fire prepared for the ungrateful, the severe punishment prepared, and the overwhelming punishment for turning from remembrance.\n\nThis follows mountains mirage to show that beyond the mirage is Hell.\n\nHell lying in ambush should not be taken as surprise without warning, as with the warner who came and they said “Allah has revealed nothing,” the keepers asking, and the Reminder for the whole world.\n\nFor the living who were nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, grateful or ungrateful, Hell ambush should make you grateful, fulfilling vows, giving food despite desire, so ambush is not for you, but salvation is, as the righteous will have salvation, Gardens, vineyards, maidens, full cups, never hearing idle talk, a generous gift from your Lord, where Hell’s ambush is avoided and the Pen writes your salvation.\n\nMore: Hell lying in ambush also indicates Hell is prepared, ready, as with chains, shackles, blazing Fire prepared for the ungrateful, the severe punishment prepared, and the overwhelming punishment for turning from remembrance. Lying in ambush, or “mirsada,” is a watch, a trap, like the garden owners’ garden watched while they slept and torment struck, and the despicable withholder watched. For the living who were nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, grateful or ungrateful, Hell ambush should make you grateful, fulfilling vows, giving food despite desire, so ambush is not for you, but salvation is, as the righteous will have salvation, Gardens, vineyards, maidens, full cups, never hearing idle talk, a generous gift from your Lord, where Hell’s ambush is avoided and the Pen writes your salvation.",
  "22": "\"as a home for the transgressors,\" defines who Hell ambushes. The transgressors are its residents.\n\n“as a home for the transgressors” translates “li-l-taghina ma’aba,” for the tyrants, transgressors, a resort, a return. Taghina, or transgressors, are those who exceed limits, as with societies that rebelled and were called to severe account, the despicable transgressor, evildoer, brute, and those who felt secure that One in heaven will not swallow. Home, or “ma’aba,” is a retreat, a dwelling, as with the raging Flame, the Blaze, the Fire whose fuel is people and stones, and the choking food, dunes, and chains seventy arms.\n\nTransgressors here are the same as the wicked asked what landed you in Hell, not praying, not feeding poor, indulging, denying until inevitable came, and the deniers woe on that Day.\n\nThis follows Hell lying in ambush to name its occupants.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think home is temporary, like the garden’s lodging for the living and the dead. Home for transgressors is where they will remain for endless ages, as next states.\n\nFor the living who love fleeting and neglect weighty Day, transgressors’ home warns to not be among those who persist in disbelief and turn away, who indulge, who feel secure that earth will not swallow, but to be among the righteous who will have salvation, whose home is Gardens, vineyards, where home is cool shade and springs, not Hell ambush.\n\nExtra: Home for the transgressors also parallels the raging Flame ripping scalps, Hell that does not let live, scorching skin, nineteen keepers, mighty catastrophe warning to humankind, and the difficult Day far from easy. Home, or “ma’aba,” is a retreat, a dwelling, like the raging Flame’s home and the Blaze. Transgressors, or “taghina,” are those who exceeded, as with societies that rebelled, the despicable transgressor, evildoer, brute, and those who felt secure that One in heaven will not swallow. For the living who love fleeting and neglect weighty Day, transgressors’ home warns to not be among those who persist in disbelief and turn away, who indulge, who feel secure, but to be among the righteous who will have salvation, whose home is Gardens, vineyards, where home is cool shade and springs, not Hell ambush.",
  "23": "\"where they will remain for ˹endless˺ ages.\" states the duration of Hell as home for transgressors. The stay is unending.\n\n“where they will remain for endless ages” translates “labithina fiha ahqaba,” remaining in it for long periods, ages, as with staying there forever for the Fire’s residents, the deviant fuel for Hell, the overwhelming punishment ascending, and the choking food. Endless ages, or “ahqaba,” are long epochs, indicating permanence for the persistent, as with the Garden under rivers to stay for ever and ever for those who believe and do good, that is ultimate triumph, and the elevated Garden where they remain.\n\nRemain for endless ages contrasts with the little while they are told to eat and enjoy as wicked, indulging and amusing until they face their Day, and the little while luxury deniers are left to Me.\n\nThis follows home for transgressors to show home’s duration.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to debate ages as finite vs infinite, missing the point that for the persistent transgressor who never believed nor prayed, denied, turned away, swaggered, and received woe, endless ages is the recompense, while for the mindful who turn in sincere repentance, forgiveness and Gardens await, and the One who is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful, worthy to be feared and entitled to forgive, can forgive before endless begins.\n\nFor practice, avoid endless ages in Hell by not transgressing, by being among the righteous who will have salvation, and by taking the Right Way while you will, reciting what is easy, establishing prayer, paying alms, lending good loan, and seeking forgiveness, so endless ages is not yours, but endless bliss in Gardens where no idle talk or lying is heard, a generous gift from your Lord.\n\nFurther: Endless ages also indicates permanence for the persistent transgressor who never believed nor prayed, denied, turned away, swaggered, and received woe, unlike the mindful who turn in sincere repentance, forgiveness and Gardens. Endless, or “ahqaba,” long epochs, shows Hell’s home is not the little while they are told to eat and enjoy as wicked, indulging until they face their Day, and the little while luxury deniers are left to Me. To avoid endless ages in Hell, be among the righteous who will have salvation, and take the Right Way while you will, recite what is easy, establish prayer, pay alms, lend good loan, and seek forgiveness, so endless ages is not yours, but endless bliss in Gardens where no idle talk or lying is heard, a generous gift from your Lord.",
  "24": "\"There they will not taste any coolness or drink,\" describes the deprivation in Hell for endless ages. The lack is total.\n\n“There they will not taste any coolness or drink” translates the transgressors’ experience where they remain, as with the Garden’s never seeing scorching heat or bitter cold, the Garden’s shade right above, fruit easy, silver vessels, crystal, ginger, Salsabil, and the people of the right’s elevated furnishings. No coolness, or “la yadhuquna fiha bardan wa la sharaba,” no cool, no drink, indicates the opposite of the Garden where cool shade and springs and any fruit they desire and full cups are, and where they are told to eat and drink happily. Bard is cool, refreshing, opposite to the scorching heat of the raging Flame that rips scalps. Drink is the pure drink flavoured with camphor, ginger, and the spring flowing at will.\n\nThis follows remain for endless ages to show what remaining entails.\n\nNo coolness or drink mirrors the smoke shade rising in three columns providing neither coolness nor shelter, sparks as huge castles and dark as black camels.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think coolness and drink are merely physical. They are also mercy, as with the Most Compassionate who holds birds and smooths earth, who gives fresh water that could be made salty and flowing water if yours sinks.\n\nFor the living who were nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, not tasting coolness or drink because of transgression should motivate tasting now the coolness of night worship more impactful and the drink of remembrance wholeheartedly, and giving rightful share, so tasting in Hell is replaced by tasting bliss and vast kingdom in Gardens held in honour, where coolness and drink are abundant, a fitting reward and generous gift.\n\nMore: No coolness or drink also describes the Garden’s never seeing scorching heat or bitter cold, the Garden’s shade right above, fruit easy, silver vessels, crystal, ginger, Salsabil, and the people of the right’s elevated furnishings. No coolness, or “la yadhuquna bardan,” no cool, opposite to the Garden where cool shade and springs and any fruit they desire and full cups are, where they are told to eat and drink happily. Drink is pure drink flavoured with camphor, ginger, and the spring flowing at will. No coolness or drink should motivate tasting now the coolness of night worship more impactful and the drink of remembrance wholeheartedly, and giving rightful share, so tasting in Hell is replaced by tasting bliss and vast kingdom in Gardens held in honour, where coolness and drink are abundant, a fitting reward and generous gift.",
  "25": "\"except boiling water and ˹oozing˺ pus—\" gives the only taste in Hell after no coolness or drink. The exception is torment.\n\n“except boiling water and oozing pus—” translates “illa hamiman wa ghassaqa,” except hot water and pus, festering discharge, as with hamim, hot, scalding, and ghassaq, cold, foul pus, the two extremes of punishment, like scorching heat and bitter cold, and as with hamim and ghassaq for the boast that honour expels inferior, and the oozing pus that none eat except evildoers, the choking food, and the painful punishment in store.\n\nBoiling water and oozing pus are the opposite of the Gardens’ pure wine flavoured with camphor, ginger, Salsabil, silver vessels precisely filled, and the Lord will give them a pure drink, and the Garden’s shade right above.\n\nThis follows no coolness or drink to show that the only taste is the worst.\n\nThe two, boiling and oozing, show the Fire combines extremes, as with the garden test’s chaff and ashes.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat boiling water and pus as metaphor for guilt. They are real, as with the raging Flame that rips scalps and the dunes.\n\nFor the one created from humble fluid, boiling water and pus warn that the One who perfectly ordained humble fluid and placed it in secure place can also ordain this. To avoid this taste, be among the righteous who will have salvation, Gardens, vineyards, maiden, full cups, never hearing idle talk, a generous gift, where taste is coolness and drink, not boiling and pus.\n\nExtra: Boiling water and oozing pus also are the opposite of the Gardens’ pure wine flavoured with camphor, ginger, Salsabil, silver vessels precisely filled, and the Lord will give them a pure drink. Boiling water, or “hamim,” hot scalding, and pus, or “ghassaq,” cold foul, are the two extremes of punishment, like scorching heat and bitter cold, and as with hamim and ghassaq for the boast. Boiling water and pus should humble the one created from humble fluid, placed in secure place, perfectly ordained, made earth a lodging, mountains pegs. To avoid this taste, be among the righteous who will have salvation, Gardens, vineyards, maiden, full cups, never hearing idle talk, a generous gift, where taste is coolness and drink, not boiling and pus.",
  "26": "\"a fitting reward.\" judges the boiling water and pus as just recompense. The fit is precise.\n\n“a fitting reward” translates “jaza’an wifaqa,” a recompense in full accordance, fitting, as with the well-preserved Record, the Pen, and the appointed time’s perfect ordainment, How excellent are We in doing so, and the Gardens held in honour where striving appreciated. Fitting indicates that boiling and pus fit the deeds, as with “So let every soul look to what it has sent forth for tomorrow” and “We have everything recorded precisely.”\n\nThis follows boiling water and pus to show justice, and precedes “For they never expected any reckoning, and totally rejected Our signs, and We have everything recorded precisely, So taste for all you will get from Us is more torment,” which details why fitting.\n\nFitting reward for Hell contrasts with a fitting reward as generous gift from your Lord for the righteous, both fitting, but one is justice for wicked, the other generosity for good-doers.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think fitting reward is vengeful excess, like the brute’s snout marked. Fitting is measured, as with crystalline silver filled precisely as desired, but here precisely as deserved.\n\nFor the living, fitting reward should motivate examination of what is sent forth, being mindful to best ability, hearing and obeying, spending, and being saved from selfishness, so fitting for you is the Gardens’ bliss and vast kingdom, not boiling water and pus, and the fitting is the generous gift, not the endless ages.\n\nFurther: Fitting reward also judges the Garden’s generous gift as fitting, both fitting, but one is justice for wicked, the other generosity for good-doers. Fitting, or “wifaqa,” as with the well-preserved Record, the Pen, and the appointed time’s perfect ordainment, How excellent are We in doing so, and the Gardens held in honour where striving appreciated. Fitting for Hell contrasts with fitting as generous gift from your Lord for the righteous, both fitting, showing that the One who placed humble fluid in secure place and perfectly ordained can fit recompense precisely, as with crystalline silver filled precisely as desired. For the living, fitting reward should motivate being mindful to best ability, hearing and obeying, spending, and being saved from selfishness, so fitting for you is the Gardens’ bliss and vast kingdom, not boiling water and pus.",
  "27": "\"For they never expected any reckoning,\" gives the first reason the boiling water and pus is fitting. The lack of expectation explains persistence.\n\n“For they never expected any reckoning” translates “innahum kanu la yarjuna hisaba,” they used not to hope for, expect, reckoning, account, as with the deniers who see the Day as far, the challenger demanding punishment bound to come, the garden owners leaving no thought for Allah’s Will, and the luxury deniers indulging until they face their Day. Never expected reckoning echoes the deniers who asked “When is the Day?” mockingly and thought Allah would not resurrect, and the despicable withholder who thought wealth proves ancient fables.\n\nThis follows fitting reward to show why fitting, and precedes totally rejected Our signs, showing two reasons.\n\nNever expected indicates they lived as if dispersed over earth will never be gathered, though to Him you will be gathered, as with the Pen writing.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think expecting reckoning is mere fear, like the distressed with evil halu‘. Expecting is hope for justice, as with the right-hand’s “I surely knew I would face my reckoning” in a life of bliss.\n\nFor practice, expect reckoning now, as with the self-reproaching soul that anticipates devastating faqi rah and the bright faces looking at their Lord, so expectation becomes preparation, protecting families, giving rightful share, walking upright, so reckoning expected becomes Gardens held in honour where you are told to eat and drink joyfully, not boiling water and pus.\n\nMore: Never expected any reckoning also describes the deniers who see the Day as far, the challenger demanding punishment bound to come, the garden owners leaving no thought for Allah’s Will, and the luxury deniers indulging until they face their Day. Never expected reckoning, or “la yarjuna hisaba,” they used not to hope for account, as with the deniers who asked “When is the Day?” mockingly and thought Allah would not resurrect, and the despicable withholder who thought wealth proves ancient fables. To expect reckoning now, be among those who were in awe without seeing with mighty reward, who firmly believe in the Day, fear punishment knowing none should feel secure, and guard chastity, so expectation becomes Gardens held in honour where you are told to eat and drink happily, not boiling water and pus.",
  "28": "\"and totally rejected Our signs.\" gives the second reason the boiling water and pus is fitting, after never expecting reckoning. The rejection was total.\n\n“and totally rejected Our signs” translates “wa kadhdhabu bi-ayatina kidhdhaba,” they denied Our signs with vehement denial, as with the deniers’ ancient fables because blessed with wealth, pure magic when the foretold prophet came, “Allah has revealed nothing, You are extremely astray,” and the despicable withholder, slanderer, gossip. Totally rejected indicates intensity, like persisting in disbelief and acting very arrogantly, pressing fingers, covering, devising tremendous plot urging idols, and leading many astray.\n\nOur signs, or “ayatina,” include the seven heavens without flaw, the Pen, the Reminder that would humble a mountain, the Light, the balance, the garden reduced to ashes while they slept, the beast, the fresh water, and the momentous news, the Day appointed.\n\nThis follows never expected reckoning to show that not expecting led to rejecting, and precedes “And We have everything recorded precisely,” showing rejection was recorded.\n\nTotally rejected contrasts with the virtuous who believed the amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance, who will never associate, and who fulfil vows.\n\nFor the one who was nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, grateful or ungrateful, totally rejecting is the ungrateful choice, whose preparation is chains, shackles, blazing Fire. To avoid totally rejecting, be among the grateful who give food despite desire for Allah alone, fear the distressful Day, and are delivered, rewarded with Garden and silk, where rejecting is replaced by “We feed you only for Allah, seeking neither reward nor thanks.”\n\nExtra: Totally rejected Our signs also shows total denial, as with the despicable withholder, slanderer, gossip-monger, withholder, transgressor, brute, and those who felt secure that One in heaven will not swallow, who persisited in arrogance and aversion, withholding good, and saying ancient fables and pure magic. Our signs, or “ayatina,” include the seven heavens without flaw, the Pen, the Reminder that would humble a mountain, the Light, the balance, the garden reduced to ashes, and the momentous news, the Day appointed. Totally rejected is intensity, like persisting in disbelief and acting very arrogantly, pressing fingers, covering, devising tremendous plot urging idols. To avoid totally rejecting, be among the grateful who believed the amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance, who will never associate, and who fulfil vows, so rejecting is replaced by Gardens held in honour where you never hear idle talk.",
  "29": "\"And We have everything recorded precisely.\" states the record that makes the fitting reward fitting and the rejection known. The verse is the documentary guarantee.\n\n“And We have everything recorded precisely” translates “wa kulla shay’in ahsaynahu kitaba,” everything We have enumerated in writing, as with the well-preserved Record only purified touch, the Pen and what everyone writes, the appointed time that never delays, the presentation where no secret stays hidden, and the informing of what was sent forth and left behind, despite excuses, the soul testifying against itself. Precisely, or “kitaba,” in a book, indicates the well-preserved Record, the Pen’s writing that is not poet or fortune-teller.\n\nThis follows totally rejected Our signs to show that rejection was recorded, and precedes “So taste for all you will get from Us is more torment,” showing that tasting is based on precise record.\n\nEverything includes humble fluid placed, secure, appointed, perfect ordainment, earth lodging, mountains pegs, pairs, sleep, night, day, heavens, lamp, rain, grain, orchards, appointed Day, Trumpet, crowds, sky gates, mountains mirage, Hell ambush, home for transgressors, endless ages, no coolness, boiling, pus.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to doubt precise recording, as with ancient fables dismissal. The Pen assures precision.\n\nFor the living who will be informed, precise recording should motivate being mindful to best ability, hearing and obeying, spending, being true to trusts, so record is the happy “Read my record” in a life of bliss, not the boiling water and pus, and the generous gift, not the fitting reward of more torment.\n\nFurther: Everything recorded precisely also states the documentary guarantee, as with the well-preserved Record only purified touch, the Pen and what everyone writes, the appointed time that never delays, the presentation where no secret stays hidden, and the informing of what was sent forth and left behind, despite excuses, the soul testifying against itself. Precisely, or “kitaba,” in a book, indicates the Record. Everything includes humble fluid placed, secure, appointed, perfect ordainment, earth lodging, mountains pegs, pairs, sleep, night, day, heavens, lamp, rain, grain, orchards, appointed Day, Trumpet, crowds, sky gates, mountains mirage, Hell ambush, home for transgressors, endless ages, no coolness, boiling, pus. To have precise record be the happy “Read my record” in a life of bliss, be mindful to best ability, hear and obey, spend, and be true to trusts.",
  "30": "\"˹So the deniers will be told,˺ “Taste ˹the punishment˺, for all you will get from Us is more torment.”\" gives the command to the transgressors after precise recording. The tasting is increased torment.\n\n“So the deniers will be told, ‘Taste the punishment, for all you will get from Us is more torment’” translates the address to those who never expected reckoning and totally rejected signs. Taste, or “dhuqu,” is to experience, as with tasting total loss, severe account, and the garden’s ashes. More torment, or “fa-lan nazidakum illa ‘adhaba,” We will not increase you except in punishment, opposite to the Gardens where good sent forth is found with Allah better and greater, the good loan multiplied, and the striving appreciated.\n\nThis follows everything recorded precisely to show that tasting is based on record and is only more, not less, as with the Fire that does not let live and the raging Flame that rips scalps.\n\nAll you will get from Us is more torment indicates that Hell’s ambush, home for transgressors, endless ages, no coolness, boiling and pus, fitting reward, are not static but increasing, as with the ascending overwhelming punishment for turning from remembrance.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear “Taste” as invitation to enjoy. Taste here is to suffer, as with oozing pus.\n\nFor practice, avoid tasting this by tasting now the camphor drink, the spring flowing at will, the ginger and Salsabil, the pure drink from your Lord, by being among the righteous who will have salvation, Gardens, vineyards, maidens, full cups, never hearing idle talk, a generous gift, so tasting becomes “Eat and drink happily for what you used to do” in cool shade and springs, where tasting is bliss and vast kingdom.\n\nMore: Taste the punishment, for all you will get from Us is more torment also shows that tasting is based on precise record and is only more, not less, as with the Fire that does not let live and the raging Flame that rips scalps. More torment indicates Hell’s ambush, home for transgressors, endless ages, no coolness, boiling and pus, fitting reward, are not static but increasing, as with the ascending overwhelming punishment for turning from remembrance. Taste here is to suffer, as with oozing pus. For practice, avoid tasting this by tasting now the camphor drink, the spring flowing at will, the ginger and Salsabil, the pure drink from your Lord, by being among the righteous who will have salvation, Gardens, vineyards, maidens, full cups, never hearing idle talk, a generous gift, so tasting becomes “Eat and drink happily for what you used to do” in cool shade and springs.",
  "31": "\"Indeed, the righteous will have salvation—\" contrasts after tasting will be told, more torment. The righteous have the opposite, salvation.\n\n“Indeed, the righteous will have salvation—” translates “inna li-l-muttaqina mafaza,” indeed for the God-conscious is a place of success, as with the ultimate triumph for those who believe and do good admitted into Gardens under rivers for ever and ever, the Gardens held in honour for the excepted who pray, and the Gardens of Bliss with their Lord. Salvation, or “mafaza,” is triumph, as with the Pen’s writing and the well-preserved Record, the weighty revelation, and the reminder to the whole world. Righteous, or “muttaqin,” are the God-conscious, the mindful to best ability who hear and obey and spend and are saved from selfishness, the virtuous who fulfil vows and give food despite desire, the excepted who pray consistently and properly observant.\n\nThis follows taste more torment to show the other path, and precedes Gardens, vineyards, maidens, full cups, no idle talk, generous gift.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think salvation is automatic for the label righteous, like honour that expels inferior. Salvation is for those who showed the Way grateful, whose striving is appreciated.\n\nFor the one created from humble fluid, salvation should motivate choosing grateful now, before the Day the Trumpet will be blown, sky gates, mountains mirage, Hell ambush, so salvation is your cool shade and springs where you are told to eat and drink happily, rewarded as good-doers, not the transgressors’ endless ages.\n\nExtra: Righteous will have salvation also parallels the Gardens held in honour for the excepted who pray, and the Gardens of Bliss with their Lord. Salvation, or “mafaza,” is triumph, as with the Pen’s writing and the well-preserved Record, the weighty revelation, and the reminder to the whole world. Righteous, or “muttaqin,” are the God-conscious, mindful to best ability who hear and obey and spend and are saved from selfishness, the virtuous who fulfil vows and give food despite desire, the excepted who pray consistently and properly observant. To be among the righteous who will have salvation, choose grateful now, before the Day the Trumpet will be blown, sky gates, mountains mirage, Hell ambush, so salvation is your cool shade and springs where you are told to eat and drink happily, not the transgressors’ endless ages.",
  "32": "\"Gardens, vineyards,\" details the salvation for the righteous after stating they will have salvation. The first elements are Gardens and vineyards.\n\n“Gardens, vineyards” translates “hada’iq wa a‘naba,” orchards, enclosed Gardens, and grapes, as with dense orchards, Gardens and vineyards, Gardens under rivers, Gardens of Bliss, elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach, and Gardens held in honour. Gardens and vineyards are the opposite of Hell lying in ambush as home for transgressors where they remain endless ages with no coolness.\n\nGardens, or “hada’iq,” are walled, lush, like the garden owners’ garden before ashes, now restored as better for the grateful, and the helpers’ gardens and rivers supplied after seeking forgiveness.\n\nVineyards, or “a‘naba,” are grapes, the select fruit, like any fruit they desire and full cups of pure wine.\n\nThis follows salvation to detail it, and precedes full-bosomed maidens of equal age and full cups, never hearing idle talk.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to reduce Gardens, vineyards to worldly orchards that could be chaff. Gardens here are the excellent provision granted to those who believe and do good for ever and ever, sincere repentance’s light.\n\nFor the human created to test, shown grateful or ungrateful, Gardens, vineyards are the grateful’s vast kingdom and bliss, where dense is not dunes but shade right above, where pouring water produces grain and plants for the grateful, so Gardens remain, while the garden that excluded poor was reduced to ashes, showing which Garden to invest in with rightful share and good loan.\n\nFurther: Gardens, vineyards also details salvation, Gardens and vineyards, orchards, enclosed Gardens, and grapes, as with dense orchards, Gardens and vineyards, Gardens under rivers, Gardens of Bliss, elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach, and Gardens held in honour. Gardens and vineyards are the opposite of Hell lying in ambush as home for transgressors where they remain endless ages with no coolness. Gardens are walled, lush, like the garden owners’ garden before ashes, now restored as better for the grateful, and the helpers’ gardens and rivers supplied after seeking forgiveness. To be among Gardens, vineyards are the grateful’s vast kingdom and bliss, where dense is not dunes but shade right above, where pouring water produces grain and plants for the grateful, so Gardens remain, while the garden that excluded poor was reduced to ashes.",
  "33": "\"and full-bosomed maidens of equal age,\" adds companionship to Gardens and vineyards for the righteous. The maidens are described as mature and peer.\n\n“and full-bosomed maidens of equal age” translates “wa kawa‘iba atraba,” youthful, fully developed maidens, peers, as with the wife of Pharaoh’s house near Allah, Mary who guarded chastity and was devout, and the better wives submissive, faithful, devout, repentant, dedicated to worship and fasting, previously married or virgins, and the full-bosomed of equal age indicates harmony, like the helpers who loved emigrants and the disciples who stood with Jesus. Equal age, or “atraba,” indicates peers, companionship, as with the Garden’s cool shade and springs where community, not isolation like no close friend on the Day, prevails.\n\nFull-bosomed indicates maturity and modesty, not objectification, as with guarding chastity within lawful bonds for the chaste who are free from blame and transgressors beyond.\n\nThis follows Gardens, vineyards to add companionship, and precedes full cups, never hearing idle talk.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to read this as mere sensuality, like the brute’s ancient fables. It is honour for the righteous who guarded chastity, were true to trusts, and walked upright.\n\nFor the grateful who were nothing, drop, Way shown, fulfilled vows, gave food despite desire, this companionship is the reward for protecting families from Fire, for being in awe without seeing, and for walking upright, so full-bosomed maidens of equal age are your companions in Gardens where you recline on canopied couches never seeing scorching heat, where the Fire’s choking food is not yours.\n\nMore: Full-bosomed maidens of equal age also adds companionship to Gardens and vineyards, youthful, fully developed maidens, peers, as with the wife of Pharaoh’s house near Allah, Mary who guarded chastity and was devout, and the better wives submissive, faithful. Equal age, or “atraba,” indicates peers, companionship, as with the Garden’s cool shade and springs where community, not isolation like no close friend on the Day, prevails. For the grateful who were nothing, drop, Way shown, fulfilled vows, gave food despite desire, this companionship is the reward for protecting families, for being in awe without seeing, and for walking upright, so full-bosomed maidens are your companions in Gardens where you recline on canopied couches never seeing scorching heat, where the Fire’s choking food is not yours.",
  "34": "\"and full cups ˹of pure wine˺,\" adds drink to Gardens, vineyards, and maidens for the righteous. The cups are full and pure.\n\n“and full cups of pure wine” translates “wa ka’san dihaqa,” a cup overflowing, full, as with the camphor drink, the spring flowing at will, crystalline silver filled precisely, ginger, Salsabil, and the pure drink from the Lord, the drink that would humble a mountain if you consider. Full, or “dihaqa,” is brimming, like the abundant rain showered, gardens and rivers supplied, and the excellent provision for ever and ever.\n\nPure wine, or “ka’s,” is the cup as with camphor and ginger, not worldly wine that intoxicates, but the Garden’s pure wine that does not let live or die, scorching.\n\nFull cups follows Gardens, vineyards, maidens to complete the Garden’s hospitality, as with shade, fruit, silver vessels.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to equate full cups with worldly intoxicant, like the despicable withholder’s ancient fables. Full cups are pure, like the well-preserved Record.\n\nFor the righteous, full cups are the reward for being true to trusts, honest in testimony, properly observant, whose Gardens are held in honour, where full cups are told to eat and drink happily, rewarded as good-doers, where no idle talk or lying is heard, a generous gift from your Lord, whose Hands hold all authority and who is Most Capable.\n\nExtra: Full cups of pure wine also adds drink to Gardens, vineyards, maidens. Full, or “dihaqa,” is brimming, like the abundant rain showered, gardens and rivers supplied, and the excellent provision for ever and ever. Pure wine, or “ka’s,” is the cup as with camphor and ginger, not worldly wine that intoxicates, but the Garden’s pure wine. Full cups follows Gardens, vineyards, maidens to complete hospitality, as with shade, fruit, silver vessels. To have full cups, be among the righteous, be true to trusts, honest in testimony, properly observant, whose Gardens are held in honour, where full cups are told to eat and drink happily, rewarded as good-doers, where no idle talk or lying is heard, a generous gift from your Lord, whose Hands hold all authority and who is Most Capable.",
  "35": "\"never to hear any idle talk or lying therein—\" describes the soundscape of the righteous’ Gardens, vineyards, maidens, full cups. The silence is from harm.\n\n“never to hear any idle talk or lying therein—” translates “la yasma‘una fiha laghwan wa la kidhdhaba,” they will not hear therein vain speech nor lying, as with the Garden where they will not hear idle talk or sin, where only peace, and the elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach and they are told to eat and drink joyfully. Idle talk, or “laghw,” is vain, as with the caravan fanfare that drew crowds from the pulpit, the rushing headlong to mock, the pressing fingers, and the despicable slander and gossip. Lying, or “kidhdhab,” is falsehood, as with the foolish uttering outrageous falsehoods, ancient fables, pure magic, and oaths as shields.\n\nNever hearing indicates the Gardens’ speech is pure, like the Pen’s truthful writing, the well-preserved Record, and the reminder.\n\nThis follows full cups to show that even with full cups, no intoxicated idle talk occurs.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think idle talk is merely silence. It is absence of harm, replaced by the Gardens’ asking one another about the wicked with gratitude.\n\nFor the living who indulge in falsehood along with others until the inevitable came, never hearing idle talk is the cure. Be among those who make private talk for goodness and righteousness, who remember the Name morning and evening, who are true to trusts, so idle talk is not your garden, but the Gardens where you never hear it, a fitting reward as generous gift from your Lord, where woe on that Day to deniers is not yours.\n\nFurther: Never to hear idle talk or lying therein also describes the soundscape, never hearing vain speech nor lying, as with the Garden where they will not hear idle talk or sin, where only peace, and the elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach and they are told to eat and drink joyfully. Idle talk, or “laghw,” is vain, as with the caravan fanfare that drew crowds, the rushing headlong to mock, the pressing fingers. Lying, or “kidhdhab,” is falsehood, as with the foolish uttering outrageous falsehoods. Never hearing indicates the Gardens’ speech is pure, like the Pen’s truthful writing, the well-preserved Record, and the reminder. For the living who indulge in falsehood along with others, never hearing idle talk is the cure. Be among those who make private talk for goodness and righteousness, who remember the Name morning and evening, who are true to trusts, so idle talk is not your garden, but the Gardens where you never hear it, a fitting reward as generous gift from your Lord, where woe on that Day to deniers is not yours.",
  "36": "\"a ˹fitting˺ reward as a generous gift from your Lord,\" concludes the salvation description after never hearing idle talk. The reward is fitting and a gift.\n\n“a fitting reward as a generous gift from your Lord” translates “jaza’an min rabbika ‘ata’an hisaba,” a recompense from your Lord, a gift, a reckoning, as with whatever good you send forth you will find with Allah better and greater, the good loan multiplied and forgiven, and the striving appreciated. Fitting, or “wifaqa,” as with the boiling water and pus fitting, but here generous gift, or “‘ata’an hisaba,” is a gift, a calculation, sufficient, as with the Gardens under rivers for ever and ever, excellent provision, splendid homes, and the vast kingdom and bliss.\n\nA generous gift from your Lord indicates the Lord who created you from humble fluid placed in secure place until appointed time, perfectly ordained, made earth a lodging, mountains pegs, pairs, sleep, night, day, heavens, lamp, rain, grain, orchards, and appointed Day, now gifts the righteous.\n\nFitting and generous gift shows justice and generosity combined, as with the Balance so people may administer justice and the Most Appreciative, Most Forbearing.\n\nThis follows never hearing idle talk to close the Gardens section.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear fitting as wage that obliges. Gift indicates favour He grants to whoever He wills, Lord of infinite bounty, yet fitting shows deeds matter.\n\nFor the one who was nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, grateful or ungrateful, fitting reward as generous gift should make you grateful, fulfilling vows, fearing sweeping horror, giving food despite desire, so gift becomes your Gardens, vineyards, maidens, full cups, no idle talk, where gift is from your Lord who holds all authority and is Most Capable, not the Smoke shade that provides neither coolness nor shelter.\n\nMore: Fitting reward as generous gift from your Lord also concludes salvation, a fitting reward as a generous gift, as with whatever good you send forth you will find with Allah better and greater, the good loan multiplied and forgiven, and the striving appreciated. Fitting, or “wifaqa,” and generous gift, or “‘ata’an hisaba,” is a gift, a reckoning, sufficient, as with the Gardens under rivers for ever and ever, excellent provision, splendid homes, and the vast kingdom and bliss. Fitting and generous gift shows justice and generosity combined, as with the Balance so people may administer justice and the Most Appreciative, Most Forbearing. For the one who was nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, grateful or ungrateful, fitting reward as generous gift should make you grateful, fulfilling vows, feeding despite desire, so gift becomes your Gardens, vineyards, maidens, full cups, no idle talk, where gift is from your Lord who holds all authority and is Most Capable, not the smoke shade that provides neither coolness nor shelter.",
  "37": "\"the Lord of the heavens and the earth and everything in between, the Most Compassionate. No one will dare speak to Him\" describes the One from whom the fitting reward and generous gift comes, the Lord whose gift is salvation, Gardens, vineyards, maidens, full cups, no idle talk.\n\n“the Lord of the heavens and the earth and everything in between, the Most Compassionate. No one will dare speak to Him” translates the Owner of the heavens smoothed like a bed, pegged with mountains, pairs, sleep, night, day, seven mighty heavens, shining lamp, pouring rain, grain, dense orchards, appointed Day, Trumpet, crowds, sky gates, mountains mirage, Hell ambush, home for transgressors, endless ages, no coolness, boiling and pus, fitting reward, never expecting reckoning, totally rejecting signs, precise recording, taste more torment, salvation, Gardens, vineyards, maiden, full cups, never idle talk, fitting gift. Lord of the heavens and the earth and everything in between indicates the Most Compassionate who holds all authority, Most Capable, who determines day and night, who is All-Knowing, All-Wise, who descends command between seven heavens.\n\nMost Compassionate, or “al-Rahman,” here emphasizes that the Day of Decision, though severe for transgressors, is administered by mercy, as with the Blessed in Whose Hands rests all authority, Most Capable, who created death and life to test.\n\nNo one will dare speak to Him indicates awe that even the angels on the sides of the torn sky and the eight bearing the Throne stand in ranks silent unless granted permission, as next states, the holy spirit and angels will stand in ranks, none will talk except those granted permission by the Most Compassionate and whose word is right.\n\nThis follows fitting reward as generous gift to show whose gift it is and why speech is guarded.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear Most Compassionate as only gentle, forgetting shackles, raging Fire, dunes. Most Compassionate is the same who warns, whose punishment none should feel secure from, yet whose mercy admits whoever He wills.\n\nFor the one created from humble fluid placed in secure place until appointed time, perfectly ordained, earth lodging, mountains pegs, the Lord of heavens and earth and in between, Most Compassionate, should make you grateful, show Way, choose grateful, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, so the Lord you will not dare speak to without permission becomes the Lord who grants you permission to speak and to be among the righteous amid cool shade and springs, told to eat and drink happily, rewarded as good-doers, not the transgressors whose home is endless ages.",
  "38": "\"on the Day the ˹holy˺ spirit and the angels will stand in ranks. None will talk, except those granted permission by the Most Compassionate and whose words will be true.\" describes the formation on the Day.\n\n“on the Day the holy spirit and the angels will stand in ranks. None will talk, except those granted permission by the Most Compassionate and whose words will be true” translates the Day of Decision’s assembly. Holy spirit, or “al-ruh,” is Gabriel, the noble spirit who delivers revelation, who ascends with angels on a Day fifty thousand years, Lord of pathways. Angels will stand in ranks, or “saffan,” rows, as with the solid ranks loved by Allah like a concrete structure, the eight bearing the Throne, and the angels on sides of the torn sky. Standing in ranks indicates order, discipline, not the rushing headlong to mock from right and left in groups.\n\nNone will talk, except those granted permission by the Most Compassionate and whose words will be true indicates that speech is licensed, like testimony honest in testimony and properly observant, not worthless planks impressive speech, not despicable slander and gossip, not the challenger demanding punishment, not the garden owners whispering to exclude poor. True words, or “sawaba,” are correct, as with the Pen and what everyone writes truthfully and the well-preserved Record.\n\nThis follows No one will dare speak to Him to detail who is silent.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think no one talks means no intercession, but “except those granted permission” allows intercession for the mindful who take the Right Way, whose pleas will benefit.\n\nFor the living who will be among those presented with no secrets hidden, standing in ranks should motivate standing now in solid ranks for the weighty revelation, reciting properly, remembering the Name wholeheartedly, taking Trustee, so standing in ranks on that Day is with the holy spirit and angels, not with the spooked zebras fleeing from the reminder.",
  "39": "\"That Day is the ˹ultimate˺ truth. So let whoever wills take the path leading back to their Lord.\" defines the Day’s nature and invites choice.\n\n“That Day is the ultimate truth. So let whoever wills take the path leading back to their Lord” translates “dhalika al-yawmu al-haqqu fa-man sha’a ittakhada ila rabbihi ma’aba,” that Day is the truth, the reality, like the Inevitable Hour that will have come to pass, the absolute truth, whose woe is repeated for deniers, and the reminder that would humble a mountain. Ultimate truth, or “al-haqqu,” is not the powerless force that would help, the honour that expels inferior, or the merchandise fanfare, but the Day fifty thousand years, the Day children’s hair turns grey, the Day the soul reaches collar bones. So let whoever wills take the path leading back to their Lord indicates volition, as with “let whoever wills take the Right Way” and “whoever wills be mindful, but they cannot unless Allah wills, He is worthy to be feared.”\n\nPath leading back, or “ma’aba,” is a return, a resort, as with Gardens, vineyards, and the cool shade and springs for the righteous who will have salvation, and the home for transgressors where they remain endless ages.\n\nThat Day is truth follows the ranks silent except permission, showing truth is not debated like “over which they disagree,” but realized.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to delay taking the path, thinking you can will later, as with wealth and children diverting and indulging until they face their Day.\n\nFor the one who was nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, grateful or ungrateful, that Day ultimate truth should make you take the path now, recite what is easy, establish prayer, pay alms, lend good loan, and seek forgiveness, so your path leads back to your Lord as Gardens held in honour where you are told to eat and drink happily, not to the raging Flame that rips scalps where you remain for endless ages and taste only boiling and pus, a fitting reward.",
  "40": "\"Indeed, We have warned you of an imminent punishment—the Day every person will see ˹the consequences of˺ what their hands have done, and the disbeliever will cry, “Oh, I wish I were dust!”\" closes Surah an-Naba with warning of imminent punishment, personal sight, and the disbeliever’s wish.\n\n“Indeed, We have warned you of an imminent punishment—the Day every person will see the consequences of what their hands have done, and the disbeliever will cry, ‘Oh, I wish I were dust!’” translates the final warning, after the Day is ultimate truth and whoever wills may take the path. Imminent punishment, or “‘adhaban qariba,” near, close, as with the challenger demanding punishment bound to come for disbelievers averted by none from the Lord of pathways, the luxury deniers left for a little while, the gardenga reduced to ashes while they slept, and the Day they see as far but We see as near. Every person will see the consequences of what their hands have done, or “ma qaddamat yadahu,” what hands put forward, as with “let every soul look to what it has sent forth for tomorrow” and “All will be informed of what they have sent forth and left behind, despite excuses, the soul is a witness against itself.” The disbeliever will cry “Oh, I wish I were dust!” like dust that mountains become mirage, earth lodging for the dead, humble fluid placed in secure place, and the garden’s dense orchards reduced to chaff, wishing to be inanimate rather than accountable.\n\nThis follows ultimate truth and path leading back to show what happens if path not taken.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear imminent as distant, like they see it as far, not near, or to think wishing to be dust helps. Wishing to be dust is regret, like woe and more woe, hasrah for disbelievers, and spooked zebras fleeing.\n\nFor the living warned of imminent punishment, see now what your hands do, being mindful to best ability, hearing and obeying, spending, being true to trusts, so the Day you see consequences is not wishing to be dust, but being among the righteous who will have salvation, Gardens, vineyards, and the generous gift from your Lord, where you see indescribable bliss and vast kingdom, not the Fire lying in ambush."
};